hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1598","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani narrated to us, al-Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was... He raised his head from bowing and did not stop standing until we saw him prostrating.\""
"1599","Ali bin Hajar told us, Maslamah bin Salih told us, and in the heart of it, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Sari’, on the authority of Amr bin Harith, he said: “I prayed Behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he raised his head from bowing, none of us would bend his back until we could see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted and sat prostrating.”"
